author ai
group gui/graph
note Where every node on the canvas ends up. The layout is recomputed from scratch every frame by Built::place_nodes; a node the reader dragged then has its position overwritten by the dragged one (App::graph_layout, in graph-draw). It works along two axes named by the graph's Direction: the main axis, across when the graph runs left to right and down when it is turned top to bottom, and the cross axis at right angles to it. Along the main axis a node sits in the lane of its Rank - its depth in the path tree, or one rank out from whatever expansion revealed it - and the lanes are laid out outward from rank 0 so the root of the path never moves. Along the cross axis the children of one node on one side are one Siblings box, stacked tightly in call order, with the box's first child level with the parent when that lane is free there and below the lane's last box otherwise; boxes in a lane never overlap and are placed breadth first, so siblings stay together however deep their own subtrees run. Each root starts a band below everything placed before it. Everything is in cells and rows (theme::Cells), which no zoom changes; pixels appear only when a rectangle is asked for with this frame's cell size.

