note The forest place_nodes walks: a path step hangs off its parent step on the callee side, an expanded node off the node that revealed it, on the caller side for callers and the callee side for callees. Each parent's callee-side children are sorted by the line of its code that names them (Built::call_line), so siblings sit in call order and the step order breaks ties; the roots are the nodes with no parent, in step order.

